Local fix to the vendored TinyUSB MTP class driver, kept here because the
submodule is a plain upstream pin (hathach/tinyusb 231347964, master of
2026-09-06) and a working-tree edit inside it is invisible to this repo.
Apply after any submodule checkout or bump:

    git -C src/usb/tinyusb apply ../tinyusb-mtp-unknown-length.patch

Guarded by PI1MHZ_MTP_SHORT_PACKET_ENDS_UNKNOWN_LENGTH_OUT (tusb_config.h).
When the host declares no length (ObjectCompressedSize 0 or 0xFFFFFFFF)
upstream ends an OUT data phase only on total_len or a ZLP, so any length
that is not a whole number of packets hangs the operation with the file
open and the LUN locked; a short packet must end the phase.  Upstream had
not changed mtp_device.c as of e97cf0296 (2026-09-08).

diff --git a/src/class/mtp/mtp_device.c b/src/class/mtp/mtp_device.c
index 275c9f858..b2011cef0 100644
--- a/src/class/mtp/mtp_device.c
+++ b/src/class/mtp/mtp_device.c
@@ -432,6 +432,21 @@ bool mtpd_xfer_cb(uint8_t rhport, uint8_t ep_addr, xfer_result_t event, uint32_t
         // OUT completion: reaching total_len or ZLP only. A short packet does NOT end the phase
         // (an early short packet before total_len is the cancel case, not normal completion).
         is_complete = (p_mtp->xferred_len >= p_mtp->total_len) || ((xferred_bytes == 0 && p_mtp->xferred_len > 0));
+#if PI1MHZ_MTP_SHORT_PACKET_ENDS_UNKNOWN_LENGTH_OUT
+        // ...EXCEPT when the length is unknown.  A host that sent
+        // ObjectCompressedSize 0 or 0xFFFFFFFF leaves the application no
+        // length to give tud_mtp_data_receive(), so total_len is UINT32_MAX
+        // and the rule above can only ever be satisfied by a ZLP - which the
+        // host sends only when its data happens to be a whole number of
+        // packets.  For every other length the transfer simply stops: the
+        // application stops re-arming, no ZLP arrives, data_complete_cb never
+        // fires and no response is ever sent, so the operation hangs with the
+        // file still open and the destination LUN still locked.  For an
+        // unknown length the short packet IS the terminator.
+        if (p_mtp->total_len == UINT32_MAX && xferred_bytes > 0 && xferred_bytes < threshold) {
+          is_complete = true;
+        }
+#endif
       }
 
       TU_LOG_DRV("  MTP Data %s CB: xferred_bytes=%lu, xferred_len/total_len=%lu/%lu, is_complete=%d\r\n",
